{"from": "claim:mk-05-01-gadarenes-region", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-08-28-country-of-gergesenes", "note": "Matthew 8:28 (KJV) reads 'Gergesenes'; Mark 5:1 in WEB reads 'Gadarenes' and the oldest manuscripts read 'Gerasenes' - the same event set in the same disputed country."}
{"from": "claim:mk-05-02-03-one-demoniac", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-08-28-demoniacs-tombs", "note": "Mark and Luke tell of one demoniac; Matthew tells of two. A number difference between Gospels, not evidence."}
{"from": "claim:mk-05-11-13-two-thousand-swine", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-08-30-herd-of-swine", "note": "Mark alone gives the size of the herd, 'about two thousand'; Matthew says only a great herd."}
{"from": "claim:mk-05-11-13-two-thousand-swine", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-08-32-swine-drowned", "note": "The drowning of the herd into the sea is the same event in both Gospels; Mark supplies the number."}
{"from": "claim:mk-05-22-23-jairus-office", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-18-ruler-office", "note": "Matthew leaves the ruler unnamed and says the daughter 'has just died'; Mark names Jairus, 'one of the rulers of the synagogue', and the daughter is only at the point of death."}
{"from": "claim:mk-05-25-26-physicians-spent-all", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-09-20-21-fringe", "note": "Both Gospels give the twelve-year haemorrhage and the touching of the garment; Mark alone adds the failed physicians and the money spent."}
